# Node modules
node_modules/

# The lockfile and the workspace definition are committed on purpose.
#
# Without the workspace file a fresh clone is not a workspace at all: `pnpm
# install` links nothing and every cross-package import fails. Without the
# lockfile each install resolves whatever is newest inside the declared ranges,
# which is how a clean reinstall once pulled a react-error-boundary that had
# changed `FallbackProps` and broke the build with no source change behind it.
#
# `pnpm-workspace.dev.yaml` and `.prod.yaml` remain as manual variants to copy
# over this file; the committed default is the dev one, so clone-install-build
# works with no extra step.

# Build output directories
dist/
build/

